      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch to double-check. \nasyncResp was truly unused in the lambda body (only in the capture list, never dereferenced), so this is safe. \n\nAsyncResp lifetime is preserved independently: the callback argument itself is a std::bind_front closure that already owns its own copy of asyncResp (see getTotalPowerSensor(): std::bind_front(handleTotalPowerList, asyncResp, chassisId)), so it keeps the response alive through the whole async chain regardless of this local capture. Marked [[maybe_unused]] per convention. \n\nAlso now confirmed end-to-end with a live GET against a real Sensor.Purpose object — PowerWatts.Reading populates correctly.",
